This average was obtained by focusing the alignment on four repeats along the central row of density. Initially, the whole, unmasked average is shown. Later, the central row of density (CD) with its contact to the peripheral rows (PR) is shown in solid grey by applying the alignment mask while the signal of the whole disk rim is displayed in transparent gray. The same representation was used in
